WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.569
"The Conjuring: The Devil Made Me Do It" is
the third installment in the horror franchise

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:09.890
centered around ghostbusting power couple
Ed and Lorraine Warren.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:14.410
Unlike the previous movies that focused more
on haunted houses, this case centers on a

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.330
demon-haunted child.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.880
Missed some of the details?

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:18.919
We'll catch you up.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:24.320
The film opens up with the exorcism of little
eight-year-old David Glatzel.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:30.239
The Warrens are in attendance, as is Arne
Johnson, who is the boyfriend of Debbie Glatzel,

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:31.550
David's big sister.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.410
It's here that Lorraine Warren touches David
and experiences her first blink-and-you'll-miss-it

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:41.550
psychic glimpse of what appears to be an altar
with a pentagram carved on it, covered candles,

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.660
and a goblet.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:47.900
In a misguided act of bravery, Arne intervenes
during the exorcism performed by Father Gordon,

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.410
and pleads for the demon to take him instead
of David.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.810
The demon obliges, but during all the chaos,
it passes into him.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:01:00.750
The only one to catch a glimpse of this body
swap is Ed, who unfortunately suffers a massive

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.480
heart attack before he is able to sound the
alarm.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.600
Days later, Arne starts experiencing demonic
hallucinations of his own, including what

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:14.780
appears to be a gaunt-faced goth librarian
who is at first simply known as the Occultist.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.400
As Ed finally regains consciousness in the
hospital, he doesn't waste a second and immediately

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.250
tells Lorraine that the demon has got Arne.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:26.000
This warning, of course, comes far too late,
and while Arne and Debbie are hanging out

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.860
with their surly landlord Bruno, the demon
seems to take the opportunity to strike.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:36.590
Arne suffers extreme hallucinations, mistakes
Bruno as a fanged minion from Hell, and stabs

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:37.590
him to death.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:43.030
Following Arne's incarceration for the murder
of Bruno, the Warrens — along with Debbie

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.020
Glatzel and a priest named Father Newman — visit
him in prison.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.280
Arne is convinced that the demon tricked him
into killing Bruno.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.560
It's at this point that the Warrens have Arne
read Bible verses and attempt to provoke the

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.119
spirit with various religious objects.

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:00.760
After witnessing no reaction, they determine
that he is not possessed.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.060
This raises some huge questions.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.500
How does this demon seem to come and go as
it pleases?

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:11.170
As Lorraine later states, "Demons don't just
disappear," so this forces the Warrens to

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:14.950
retrace their steps and circle back to the
Glatzel house.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:19.650
David Glatzel's very first demonic encounter
took place in the guest room, where he was

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.160
attacked by a dark spirit lurking within the
waterbed.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:27.660
After Ed observes rotted wood on the floor
that doesn't appear to be from water damage,

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.140
Lorraine makes her way under the house and
discovers a gooey black substance dripping

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:37.340
from the ceiling, as well as a unique type
of witch's totem derived from animal bones.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:41.310
And surprise, surprise, it's positioned directly
under the guest room.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:46.230
We then learn that this particular totem is
often used by master Satanists to inflict

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.319
a three-phase curse on someone.

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:50.350
In phase one, a demon is summoned.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.770
In phase two, the possessed individual takes
a life.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.660
Finally, in phase 3, the demon departs.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:01.239
All of this explains why Arne was able to
read from the Bible without exhibiting any

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:06.489
demonic reactions, but it also raises the
crucial question of who made and placed all

00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:07.830
these totems in the house.

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:14.510
The Warrens receive a tip about a priest who's
an expert on the occult and Satanic rituals.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:19.870
His name is Father Kastner, and much like
the Warrens, he has a chamber of demonic relics

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:20.910
of his own.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:25.120
After seeing a photo of the totem discovered
under the Glatzel residence, he knows exactly

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.959
who the Warrens are up against.

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:32.050
The totem is commonly used by a cult known
as the Disciples of the Ram — a fun nod

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:36.849
that "Conjuring" universe enthusiasts will
recognize as the name of the same cult from

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.030
the "Annabelle" movies.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:44.300
Kastner warns the Warrens that these sophisticated
Satanists aren't adversaries to be taken lightly.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:49.310
As we discover later in the film, the mystery
occultist pulling all the strings is indeed

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:54.980
the gaunt-faced woman we saw earlier — Lola,
who also happens to be Kastner's very own

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.069
estranged daughter, who he raised and kept
in secret from the priesthood.

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:05.120
At a young age, Lola took up some of her father's
interests and developed a dark obsession for

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.879
witchcraft and the occult.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:10.970
She's been operating within the tunnels beneath
his farmhouse the entire time.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:15.690
When the Warrens first question Kastner about
the Satanists' rituals and ask why they'd

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:21.410
target a little boy earlier in the movie,
he shrugs it off, explaining, "why is irrelevant."

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:26.150
He claims that there is no method to the madness
— the Satanists are simply organizers of

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:30.880
chaos who worship the Devil and offer him
blood sacrifices at random.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.410
As we come to find out later, his explanation
made an effort to conceal the involvement

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:37.130
and identity of his daughter.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.870
During the third act, when he finally confesses
to Lorraine that his daughter has been the

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:45.400
mastermind behind these curses, we finally
discover the meaning of her grand scheme.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.949
Drew, the trusty sidekick of the Warrens,
discovers a Latin language passage within

00:04:50.949 --> 00:04:53.580
the pages of an ancient book of witchcraft.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:59.169
The scripture talks of a curse that says the
inflicted must kill someone, then kill themselves.

00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:04.740
Once the curse is started, it must be completed
at all costs — Lola's soul depends on it.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.330
Since Drew's Latin is a bit rusty, Lorraine
opts to take the book to Kastner for a full

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.360
translation.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:15.690
As Kastner deciphers the Latin passages, it
is discovered that three sacrifices are required

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:21.570
for Lola to complete the ritual: purity, love,
and faith, or the child, the lover, and finally

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:25.620
the man of God, which explains the three totems
that are in play.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:30.330
The first is the one found under the Glatzel
house, which ultimately inflicted Arne — the

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.330
lover.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:35.449
The second was discovered by detectives in
Danvers, Massachusetts who stumbled upon the

00:05:35.449 --> 00:05:40.340
totem while piecing together the murder of
Katie Lincoln and the missing prime suspect,

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.250
her own best friend Jessica Louise Strong
— the child.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:48.790
And as you may have already guessed, the holy
man is indeed Ed Warren, who starts seeing

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:54.440
visions of a grotesque reanimated corpse and
nearly attacks Lorraine during an intense

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.350
hallucination within the confines of their
home.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:02.210
The third totem was the one found in a vase
of wilted flowers that was sent to the Warrens'

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.780
house after Ed's heart attack.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.360
But was he the originally intended third target
all along?

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.590
Earlier in the movie, you may recall that
Lorraine had brief psychic glimpses of what

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:16.690
Lola was up to whenever she laid hands on
a cursed individual.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:21.660
It happened when she touched David and Arne,
but linking with the corpse of Jessica Strong

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.280
gives her the biggest clues of all.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.800
"Ed, something terrible happened here."

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:32.300
After Lorraine uses her psychic abilities
to relive the tragic death of Katie by visiting

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:36.720
the site of her death, she not only discovers
that Katie did indeed perish at the hands

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.890
of her friend Jessica, but that afterward,
Jessica threw herself over a nearby cliff.

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:46.729
This confirms that Arne isn't exactly in the
clear, which is why he continues to be plagued

00:06:46.729 --> 00:06:51.680
by the demon in prison — it wants to drive
him to suicide in order to complete the task

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.030
it was summoned for.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:57.680
There's also a moment when Lorraine theorizes
that these demons aren't acting of their own

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.850
free will and suggests that touching the corpse
of the curse-afflicted Jessica Strong may

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:07.530
once again give her a glimpse into Lola's
lair with the mysterious altar.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.250
Her theory proves to be correct, but that
glimpse comes with a price.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:15.310
The connection works both ways — so when
Lorraine uses her clairvoyant abilities to

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:20.610
touch Jessica's corpse and see what Lola is
up to, Lola also senses Lorraine's psychic

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.210
presence and can see what she sees.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.389
Think of it as a two-way crystal ball.

00:07:25.389 --> 00:07:29.160
This possibly explains why Lola sent flowers
to the Warren household.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:34.610
While it's never exactly clear as to how long
she's been aware of the Warrens' meddling,

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:39.490
one can assume that inflicting Ed with the
curse was a sort of payback, and he just so

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:44.620
happened to conveniently fit the bill for
her third required sacrifice, the holy man.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:49.501
In fact, Lola's plans may have gone down in
an entirely different way had the Warrens

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:51.870
never intervened in the first place.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:57.199
One can assume that David Glatzel was originally
intended to be the "child of purity" sacrifice,

00:07:57.199 --> 00:07:58.460
followed by Arne, the lover.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:02.970
But when Arne pleaded for the demon to take
him, Lola had to improvise and sought out

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:06.090
a fresh new virgin victim with Jessica Strong.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:11.100
It's also quite possible that Father Gordon
or even her own estranged father, Father Kastner,

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:16.520
could've easily been the originally intended
holy man — but when those meddling Warrens

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.020
spoiled her plans, she chose to inflict the
curse on Ed.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:24.770
Either way, Lola had options, and she's clearly
the puppet master controlling the demon's

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:29.780
every move, and she can strike any cursed
individual at any time — as long as she's

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:32.159
at her infernal altar, that is.

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:37.499
Moments before his slasher-style murder at
the hands of Lola, Father Kastner reveals

00:08:37.499 --> 00:08:40.369
that the altar is the source of Lola's power.

00:08:40.369 --> 00:08:44.899
Destroying it will break the curse and vanquish
the demon's grasp over Ed and Arne.

00:08:44.899 --> 00:08:49.839
Armed with a sledgehammer, Ed narrowly pulls
this off as Lola makes one last attempt to

00:08:49.839 --> 00:08:54.630
use her diabolical mind tricks to fool him
into eliminating his own wife.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:58.589
But the love and bond between the Warrens
proves to be too strong.

00:08:58.589 --> 00:09:03.499
As Lorraine puts it, "She thinks our love
is a weakness, but it's not — it's our strength."

00:09:03.499 --> 00:09:08.079
Ed breaks free from the demon's grasp and
strikes down the altar instead of his wife.

00:09:08.079 --> 00:09:12.709
Naturally, the demon isn't too pleased with
Lola either, seeing as how she failed at her

00:09:12.709 --> 00:09:16.019
task of delivering the final two cursed souls.

00:09:16.019 --> 00:09:19.639
So instead, the demon decides, her soul will
have to do.

00:09:19.639 --> 00:09:24.470
The demon mangles her body on the spot — ding
dong, the witch is dead.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.730
Once again, it's a happy ending for the Warrens.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:31.829
We see Ed place the goblet that Lola used
to summon and control her demon placed on

00:09:31.829 --> 00:09:37.970
a shelf near the Annabelle doll in the Warrens'
ever-growing collection of supernatural artifacts.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.970
As the movie closes, we get a final shot of
them with a freshly built gazebo in their

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:47.130
backyard, which is a callback to an earlier
story that Lorraine tells Father Gordon while

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.470
they're in the hospital after Ed's heart attack.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:53.759
Thirty years ago, Ed and Lorraine first met
in a movie theater when she was 17 years old.

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:58.529
They went out for ice cream and it started
to rain, so Ed took her to a nearby gazebo

00:09:58.529 --> 00:10:00.190
where they shared their first kiss.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:03.790
It was the moment that marked the beginning
of their undying love.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:08.639
The relationship between this unique, driven
husband-and-wife couple is without a doubt

00:10:08.639 --> 00:10:12.910
the emotional center of "The Conjuring: The
Devil Made Me Do It" — as well as the beating

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:16.260
heart of the "Conjuring" series of movies
in general.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:20.889
As for Arne Johnson, while there were a bulk
of creative liberties taken regarding his

00:10:20.889 --> 00:10:26.290
supernatural exploits behind bars, his real-life
story after the events that inspired "The

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:31.040
Conjuring: The Devil Made Me Do It" reportedly
proceeded in much the same way as the movie

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.040
implied.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:37.019
Arne was ultimately charged with first-degree
manslaughter and was slammed with a 10-to-20-year

00:10:37.019 --> 00:10:41.290
prison sentence, but he was released from
prison after only serving five.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:45.569
He married his wife while he was in prison
and they are still married to this day.

00:10:45.569 --> 00:10:49.999
While the ending to their love story might
not be as bright and cheery as the Warrens',

00:10:49.999 --> 00:10:55.410
it's clear that even after being faced with
such a traumatic ordeal, their love too ultimately

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:56.440
endured.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.630
